<%# The callout's dismiss, in one place because the same callout appears on the trading floor and on
    the portfolio and a second copy is how the two would drift apart.

    A `button_to`, not `data-controller="dismiss"`. The flash close is client-side because a flash is
    an event that has already been read; this is page state that is still true, so hiding it in the
    browser would bring it straight back on the next page load and read as broken. The round trip
    writes a `dismissals` row, which Portfolio#trading_off_notice? compares against the classroom's
    trading_disabled_at - so the dismissal covers this switch-off and not the next one.

    button_to renders its own <form>, which is safe on both of these pages: the callout sits between
    sections, never inside another form. That is not true everywhere - the callout in
    admin/teachers/_form is inside the teacher form, where a nested form would be dropped by the
    parser and the button would silently submit the outer one - which is why this is passed per call
    site rather than built into the component. %>
<%= button_to dismissals_path,
              params: { key: Dismissal::TRADING_OFF },
              class: ghost_class do %>
  <%= lucide_icon "x", class: "size-4 shrink-0" %>
  Dismiss
<% end %>
